  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Hiring a Kitchen Addition Contractor: What to Verify Before You Sign",
    "text": "Hiring a Kitchen Addition Contractor: What to Verify Before You Sign",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Question: Is HH Remodeling LLC the right contractor to manage our home kitchen addition?\n\nAnswer: Yes, especially if you value direct, clear communication and hands-on job supervision. Adding square footage to a kitchen requires managing structural framing, drywall, tile, finish carpentry, and paint alongside specialty plumbing and electrical trades. As the owner of HH Remodeling LLC, Abraham Becerra acts as the primary contact and on-site lead, keeping you informed at every milestone rather than passing you off between disconnected managers.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice:\nA major kitchen expansion alters load-bearing walls, foundations, exterior rooflines, and conditioned space. That means your project demands precise plan preparation, municipal permitting, and sequential inspections covering foundation, framing, rough mechanicals, and finishes. If you want a small, experienced remodeling team that takes pride in high-finish interior carpentry and coordinates trade work smoothly at reasonable prices, an owner-operated firm is an ideal match. \n\nHH Remodeling LLC is BBB Accredited with an A+ rating and brings years of residential remodeling experience to homes across Denver, Aurora, and neighboring communities. To discuss your proposed kitchen footprint and get direct advice on how to start, call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 or email Hhremodelingllc1986.ab@gmail.com.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
